    <h2>Introduction to Sand and Crush</h2>

    <p>
        Sand and crush are essential construction materials used in residential,
        commercial and infrastructure projects. They are important ingredients
        in concrete, mortar, foundations, flooring and other construction work.
    </p>

    <p>
        Choosing suitable construction materials is important for achieving
        consistent quality and long-term durability. In Islamabad and Rawalpindi,
        builders and contractors should consider material cleanliness, grading,
        size and suitability before purchasing sand and crush.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight">
        <strong>Important:</strong> Always select sand and aggregate according
        to the project's approved specifications and the advice of a qualified
        construction engineer.
    </div>

    <h2>1. What Is Construction Sand?</h2>

    <p>
        Construction sand is a fine aggregate used in concrete, plastering,
        masonry and mortar preparation. Its quality can affect the workability
        and performance of construction mixtures.
    </p>

    <h3>Common Types of Construction Sand</h3>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>Chenab Sand</h3>
        <p>
            Chenab sand is a commonly used construction sand in Pakistan.
            Depending on its grading and cleanliness, it can be considered
            for different masonry and concrete applications.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>Lawrencepur Sand</h3>
        <p>
            Lawrencepur sand is another familiar option in the local
            construction market. Its suitability depends on its particle
            size, cleanliness and the requirements of the construction work.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>Sand for Plastering</h3>
        <p>
            Plastering requires appropriately graded and clean sand to help
            produce a smooth, consistent finish. Excessive clay, silt and
            unwanted impurities should be avoided.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>2. What Is Crush (Crushed Stone Aggregate)?</h2>

    <p>
        Crush, also known as crushed stone aggregate, is produced by breaking
        larger rocks into smaller pieces. It is widely used in concrete,
        foundations, flooring, road construction and other building applications.
    </p>

    <h3>Common Types of Crush</h3>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>3/4-Inch Crush (20 mm)</h3>
        <p>
            This aggregate size is commonly used in reinforced concrete
            applications such as beams, columns, slabs and foundations,
            depending on the approved mix design.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>1/2-Inch Crush</h3>
        <p>
            Half-inch crush is a smaller aggregate size used in selected
            concrete and construction applications where the project
            specifications require it.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="material-card">
        <h3>Bajri</h3>
        <p>
            Bajri is a commonly used local term for gravel or aggregate.
            Its size, grading and intended use should be confirmed before
            placing an order.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2>3. Uses of Sand and Crush in Construction</h2>

    <p>These materials are used in many stages of construction work:</p>

    <ul>
        <li><strong>Concrete preparation:</strong> Sand and crush are key ingredients in many concrete mixes.</li>
        <li><strong>Foundation work:</strong> Suitable aggregates are used in structural and foundation applications.</li>
        <li><strong>Roof slabs:</strong> Specified aggregate is used in reinforced concrete slab work.</li>
        <li><strong>Flooring:</strong> Sand and aggregate are used in different floor construction activities.</li>
        <li><strong>Plastering:</strong> Properly graded sand is used to prepare plaster mortar.</li>
        <li><strong>Road construction:</strong> Crushed stone is used in road base and pavement layers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How to Choose Quality Sand and Crush</h2>

    <p>
        Before purchasing materials for your project, consider these
        important quality factors:
    </p>

    <ol>
        <li><strong>Cleanliness:</strong> Check for excessive dust, clay and unwanted impurities.</li>
        <li><strong>Proper grading:</strong> Select particle sizes suitable for the intended application.</li>
        <li><strong>Material consistency:</strong> Check that the supplied material meets your requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Project specifications:</strong> Follow the mix design and technical requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery arrangements:</strong> Confirm quantity, transport and delivery timing.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>5. Sand and Crush for Projects in Islamabad & Rawalpindi</h2>

